#!/bin/bash
# B0: train the SAE with the unchanged upstream objective (MSE + dead-latent aux, k=32, x32, lr 5e-5,
# batch 4096). Upstream ships no trained checkpoint, so this is the baseline every P2 row starts from.
# qsub -P personal-riddhima scripts/nscc/baseline.pbs     (STEPS=... to change; 200k steps ~ 88 passes)
#PBS -N p2_B0
#PBS -q normal
#PBS -l select=1:ncpus=16:ngpus=1:mem=110gb
#PBS -l walltime=24:00:00
#PBS -j oe
source "$PBS_O_WORKDIR/scripts/nscc/env.sh"
set -euo pipefail
python -m p2.train --data-dir "$DATA" --val-qrels "$RAW/split/validation.qrels" \
    --output "$CKPT/B0_upstream_objective" --rank-loss none --steps "${STEPS:-200000}" \
    --eval-every 20000 --in-ram --device cuda
